  "title": "Shared Database Anti-Pattern",
  "description": "Understand why shared database is an anti-pattern.",
  "order": 2,
  "difficulty": "advanced",
  "estimatedMinutes": 17,
  "tags": ["shared-database", "anti-pattern"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "data": {
        "text": "A shared database between services is an anti-pattern. It creates tight coupling and violates service autonomy."
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Key Concepts"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "key-terms",
      "data": {
        "terms": [
          {
            "term": "Shared Database",
            "definition": "Multiple services accessing the same database."
          },
          {
            "term": "Tight Coupling",
            "definition": "Services depend on each other through shared state."
          },
          {
            "term": "Service Autonomy",
            "definition": "The ability of a service to change independently."
          },
          {
            "term": "Schema Coupling",
            "definition": "Coupling through shared database schema."
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Why It Is an Anti-Pattern"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Services cannot change schema independently",
          "Deployments become coupled",
          "Data ownership is unclear",
          "Changes require coordination"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Signs of Shared Database"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Multiple services query the same tables",
          "Services join across service data",
          "Schema changes require coordinating teams",
          "Services break when another team changes schema"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "When It Is Acceptable"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "bullet-list",
      "data": {
        "items": [
          "Read-only reporting databases",
          "Legacy systems during migration",
          "With strict schema contracts",
          "As an interim step"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "How to Fix"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "data": {
        "level": 2,
        "text": "Architecture"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "mermaid",
